# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Full quantum state tomography of an $N$-qubit system requires exponentially many measurements to estimate all $4^N -1$ independent parameters of the density matrix. For a system of 50 qubits, for example, this process requires on the order of $10^{30}$ shots, which is more than a billion times the number of stars in the observable universe. Shadow tomography [\\[1\\]](#references) is a quantum information protocol that constructs a “classical shadow” of the quantum state, from which target observables can be estimated by using a number of shots that scales logarithmically in the number of observables and is independent of system size $N$, making it relevant across many areas in quantum computing, including energy estimation, entanglement entropy and correlation function calculations, kernel estimation in quantum machine learning, and others.\n"
msgstr "Tomografi keadaan kuantum penuh bagi sistem $N$-qubit memerlukan pengukuran yang banyak secara eksponen untuk menganggar semua $4^N -1$ parameter bebas bagi matriks ketumpatan. Bagi sistem 50 qubit, sebagai contoh, proses ini memerlukan kira-kira $10^{30}$ shot, iaitu lebih daripada satu bilion kali bilangan bintang di alam semesta yang boleh diperhatikan. Tomografi bayangan [\\[1\\]](#references) ialah protokol maklumat kuantum yang membina “bayangan klasik” bagi keadaan kuantum, yang daripadanya observable sasaran boleh dianggar menggunakan bilangan shot yang berskala secara logaritma dengan bilangan observable dan tidak bergantung pada saiz sistem $N$, menjadikannya relevan merentasi banyak bidang dalam pengkomputeran kuantum, termasuk anggaran tenaga, pengiraan entropi keterkaitan dan fungsi korelasi, anggaran kernel dalam pembelajaran mesin kuantum, dan lain-lain.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial shows how to use shadow tomography to estimate local observables, such as the single-qubit magnetization $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ for qubit $i$, the two-point correlation function $\\langle Z_i Z_j\\rangle$, and the two-qubit reduced density matrix (2-RDM), of the highly entangled Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger (GHZ) state. The tutorial first illustrates a small-scale shadow tomography workflow on a 10-qubit GHZ state by using statevector simulation. Then it shows a 100-qubit demonstration on real quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menunjukkan cara menggunakan tomografi bayangan untuk menganggar observable tempatan, seperti magnetisasi qubit tunggal $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ bagi qubit $i$, fungsi korelasi dua titik $\\langle Z_i Z_j\\rangle$, dan matriks ketumpatan terturun dua-qubit (2-RDM), bagi keadaan Greenberger-Horne-Zeilinger (GHZ) yang sangat terkait. Tutorial ini mula-mula menggambarkan aliran kerja tomografi bayangan berskala kecil pada keadaan GHZ 10-qubit menggunakan simulasi statevector. Kemudian ia menunjukkan demonstrasi 100-qubit pada perkakasan kuantum sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shadow tomography protocol {#shadow-tomography-protocol}"
msgstr "Protokol tomografi bayangan {#shadow-tomography-protocol}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The shadow tomography protocol has the following steps:\n"
"1. Apply a random unitary $U$, drawn from a unitary ensemble, to the initial quantum state.\n"
"2. Measure the outcome in the computational basis, obtaining a bitstring $\\ket{b}$.\n"
"3. Store the classical snapshot, $\\hat{\\rho} = \\mathcal{M}^{-1}(U^{\\dagger}\\ket{b}\\bra{b}U)$, where $\\mathcal{M}^{-1}$ is the inverse of the measurement channel $\\mathcal{M}(\\rho)=\\mathbb{E}[U^{\\dagger}\\ket{b}\\bra{b}U]$.\n"
"4. Repeat the process $T$ times, where the collection of $T$ snapshots $\\{\\hat{\\rho}_t\\}$ forms a classical shadow $S(\\rho, T)$.\n"
"5. Estimate observable $o$ of operator $O$ as $\\frac{1}{T}\\sum_{t=1}^{T}\\text{Tr}(O\\hat{\\rho}_t)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Protokol tomografi bayangan mempunyai langkah berikut:\n"
"1. Gunakan unitari rawak $U$, yang diambil daripada ensemble unitari, pada keadaan kuantum awal.\n"
"2. Ukur hasilnya dalam asas pengiraan, untuk mendapatkan rentetan bit $\\ket{b}$.\n"
"3. Simpan snapshot klasik, $\\hat{\\rho} = \\mathcal{M}^{-1}(U^{\\dagger}\\ket{b}\\bra{b}U)$, dengan $\\mathcal{M}^{-1}$ ialah songsangan saluran pengukuran $\\mathcal{M}(\\rho)=\\mathbb{E}[U^{\\dagger}\\ket{b}\\bra{b}U]$.\n"
"4. Ulang proses ini sebanyak $T$ kali, dengan koleksi $T$ snapshot $\\{\\hat{\\rho}_t\\}$ membentuk bayangan klasik $S(\\rho, T)$.\n"
"5. Anggarkan observable $o$ bagi pengendali $O$ sebagai $\\frac{1}{T}\\sum_{t=1}^{T}\\text{Tr}(O\\hat{\\rho}_t)$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shadow tomography variants {#shadow-tomography-variants}"
msgstr "Varian tomografi bayangan {#shadow-tomography-variants}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The choice of the unitary ensemble, that is, basis, in step 1 of the protocol, affects the sample complexity, variance of estimates, and information completeness of a given shadow tomography. Many ensemble groups have been considered in the literature, each with trade-offs between complexity and observable estimation efficiency. The properties of the most commonly used variants are summarized in the following table, although this list is not exhaustive.\n"
msgstr "Pilihan ensemble unitari, iaitu asas, dalam langkah 1 protokol, mempengaruhi kompleksiti sampel, varians anggaran, dan kelengkapan maklumat bagi sesuatu tomografi bayangan. Banyak kumpulan ensemble telah dipertimbangkan dalam literatur, masing-masing dengan pertukaran antara kompleksiti dan kecekapan penganggaran observable. Sifat varian yang paling biasa digunakan diringkaskan dalam jadual berikut, walaupun senarai ini tidak lengkap.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Variant | Ensemble | Sample complexity | Circuit depth | Suitable observables |\n"
"| ------------ | ---------------------------------| ---------| ---| -------- |\n"
"| local Pauli [\\[1\\]](#references) | single-qubit Paulis $\\{X, Y, Z\\}$ | $\\mathcal{O}(3^k\\text{log}M/\\varepsilon^2)$ | 1 | local/few-body |\n"
"| global Clifford [\\[1\\]](#references) | $N$-qubit Clifford |$\\mathcal{O}(\\text{Tr}(O^2)\\text{log}M/\\varepsilon^2)$ | $\\mathcal{O}(N\\text{log}N)$ | low-rank, fidelity |\n"
"| fermionic Gaussian [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references)| matchgate circuits | $\\mathcal{O}(\\binom{\\mu}{k}\\frac{1}{\\varepsilon^2})$  | $\\mathcal{O}(N^2)$ | fermionic |\n"
"| shallow shadows [\\[4\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references) | low-depth circuits| $\\mathcal{O}(k2^k\\text{log}M/\\varepsilon^2)$ | $\\mathcal{O}(\\text{log}N)$ | non-local (hardware-friendly) |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Varian | Ensemble | Kompleksiti sampel | Kedalaman litar | Observable yang sesuai |\n"
"| ------------ | ---------------------------------| ---------| ---| -------- |\n"
"| Pauli tempatan [\\[1\\]](#references) | Pauli qubit tunggal $\\{X, Y, Z\\}$ | $\\mathcal{O}(3^k\\text{log}M/\\varepsilon^2)$ | 1 | tempatan/beberapa-jasad |\n"
"| Clifford global [\\[1\\]](#references) | Clifford $N$-qubit |$\\mathcal{O}(\\text{Tr}(O^2)\\text{log}M/\\varepsilon^2)$ | $\\mathcal{O}(N\\text{log}N)$ | pangkat rendah, fidelity |\n"
"| Gaussian fermion [\\[2\\]](#references), [\\[3\\]](#references)| litar matchgate | $\\mathcal{O}(\\binom{\\mu}{k}\\frac{1}{\\varepsilon^2})$  | $\\mathcal{O}(N^2)$ | fermion |\n"
"| bayangan cetek [\\[4\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references) | litar kedalaman rendah| $\\mathcal{O}(k2^k\\text{log}M/\\varepsilon^2)$ | $\\mathcal{O}(\\text{log}N)$ | bukan tempatan (mesra perkakasan) |\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The terms used in the table are defined as follows:\n"
msgstr "Istilah yang digunakan dalam jadual ditakrifkan seperti berikut:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "\"sample complexity\" refers to the number of measurements needed for a given shadow tomography variant.\n"
msgstr "\"kompleksiti sampel\" merujuk kepada bilangan pengukuran yang diperlukan untuk sesuatu varian tomografi bayangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "\"circuit depth\" describes how expensive the measurements are to implement on quantum hardware.\n"
msgstr "\"kedalaman litar\" menggambarkan betapa mahalnya pengukuran untuk dilaksanakan pada perkakasan kuantum.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$N$ is the number of qubits.\n"
msgstr "$N$ ialah bilangan qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$k$ is the locality of the observable (for example, $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ has $k=1$ and $\\langle Z_i Z_j\\rangle$ has $k=2$).\n"
msgstr "$k$ ialah kelokalan observable (sebagai contoh, $\\langle Z_i \\rangle$ mempunyai $k=1$ dan $\\langle Z_i Z_j\\rangle$ mempunyai $k=2$).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$M$ is the number of observables to be estimated simultaneously.\n"
msgstr "$M$ ialah bilangan observable yang hendak dianggar serentak.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\varepsilon$ is the additive error tolerance.\n"
msgstr "$\\varepsilon$ ialah toleransi ralat aditif.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$\\mu$ is the number of fermions.\n"
msgstr "$\\mu$ ialah bilangan fermion.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Though the local Pauli ensemble is the most hardware-friendly, it pays a $3^k$ sample complexity penalty, which makes it ill-suited for non-local property estimation. More generally, the local-shadow sample-complexity bound scales as $4^k$, improving to $3^k$ in the special case of tensor-product observables.\n"
msgstr "Walaupun ensemble Pauli tempatan paling mesra perkakasan, ia menanggung penalti kompleksiti sampel $3^k$, yang menjadikannya kurang sesuai untuk penganggaran sifat bukan tempatan. Secara lebih umum, had kompleksiti sampel bayangan tempatan berskala sebagai $4^k$, bertambah baik kepada $3^k$ dalam kes khas observable hasil darab tensor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conversely, while the global Clifford ensemble can be used to estimate non-local observables, its circuit depth is not favorable. Fermionic Gaussian shadows offer utility in simulations of many-body physics, chemistry, and materials, but require matchgate circuits, which might carry significant overhead on general purpose gate-based devices.\n"
msgstr "Sebaliknya, walaupun ensemble Clifford global boleh digunakan untuk menganggar observable bukan tempatan, kedalaman litarnya tidak menguntungkan. Bayangan Gaussian fermion menawarkan kegunaan dalam simulasi fizik banyak-jasad, kimia, dan bahan, tetapi memerlukan litar matchgate, yang mungkin membawa overhead yang ketara pada peranti berasaskan gate tujuan am.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shallow shadows has a circuit depth between the local Pauli and global Clifford, making it a highly promising variant for practical implementation, though there are still some open questions regarding optimal circuit depth for a given observable.\n"
msgstr "Bayangan cetek mempunyai kedalaman litar di antara Pauli tempatan dan Clifford global, menjadikannya varian yang sangat menjanjikan untuk pelaksanaan praktikal, walaupun masih terdapat beberapa persoalan terbuka tentang kedalaman litar optimum bagi sesuatu observable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As the frontier of shadow tomography research continues expanding, some of the most relevant problems to address include optimally choosing the measurement ensemble for a target set of observables, improving sample complexity bounds, and extending the protocol to time-evolved observables. Nonetheless, shadow tomography still presents one of the leading workflows for extracting maximal classical information from a quantum state using a minimum number of measurements, which makes it ideal for characterizing quantum states at scale where both full tomography and classical simulation are impossible.\n"
msgstr "Apabila sempadan penyelidikan tomografi bayangan terus berkembang, antara masalah yang paling relevan untuk ditangani termasuk memilih ensemble pengukuran secara optimum bagi set observable sasaran, menambah baik had kompleksiti sampel, dan memperluas protokol kepada observable yang berevolusi masa. Walau bagaimanapun, tomografi bayangan masih merupakan salah satu aliran kerja terkemuka untuk mengekstrak maklumat klasik maksimum daripada keadaan kuantum menggunakan bilangan pengukuran minimum, menjadikannya ideal untuk mencirikan keadaan kuantum pada skala di mana tomografi penuh dan simulasi klasik kedua-duanya mustahil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The local Pauli ensemble {#the-local-pauli-ensemble}"
msgstr "Ensemble Pauli tempatan {#the-local-pauli-ensemble}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses the random Pauli basis, that is, single-qubit Clifford gates, to collect shadows and estimate properties of the GHZ state. Note that the Pauli measurements are a great choice for estimating local observables (such as spin density, local correlation functions, and position probability density), but not global ones (such as total energy, momentum, and charge).\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini menggunakan asas Pauli rawak, iaitu gate Clifford qubit tunggal, untuk mengumpul bayangan dan menganggar sifat keadaan GHZ. Perhatikan bahawa pengukuran Pauli ialah pilihan yang sangat baik untuk menganggar observable tempatan (seperti ketumpatan spin, fungsi korelasi tempatan, dan ketumpatan kebarangkalian kedudukan), tetapi tidak untuk yang global (seperti jumlah tenaga, momentum, dan cas).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here, a random Pauli basis $\\{X, Y, Z\\}$ per qubit is independently chosen and the corresponding single-qubit rotation is applied, followed by measurement:\n"
msgstr "Di sini, asas Pauli rawak $\\{X, Y, Z\\}$ bagi setiap qubit dipilih secara bebas dan putaran qubit tunggal yang sepadan digunakan, diikuti dengan pengukuran:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "$$\n"
msgstr "$$\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"U = U_0 \\otimes U_1 \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes U_{n-1}, U_q \\in \\{I, H, S^{\\dagger}H\\}\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"U = U_0 \\otimes U_1 \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes U_{n-1}, U_q \\in \\{I, H, S^{\\dagger}H\\}\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this ensemble, the measurement channel's inverse is:\n"
msgstr "Bagi ensemble ini, songsangan saluran pengukuran ialah:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\hat{\\rho}_q=3U_q^{\\dagger}\\ket{b_q}\\bra{b_q}U_q - I\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{equation}\n"
"\\hat{\\rho}_q=3U_q^{\\dagger}\\ket{b_q}\\bra{b_q}U_q - I\n"
"\\end{equation}\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The factor of $3$ comes from averaging over the three Pauli bases, which produces a depolarizing channel with parameter $\\frac{1}{3}$. The full estimator then factorizes as a product of single-qubit estimators. As shown in the table, for $M$ observables, each of locality $k$, the number of Pauli shadows needed to estimate all observables to additive error $\\varepsilon$ with high probability is $\\mathcal{O}(\\frac{3^k\\text{log}(M)}{\\varepsilon^2})$. The system size does not affect the measurement cost as long as the observables remain local, so exponentially many observables can be estimated simultaneously with only logarithmic cost.\n"
msgstr "Faktor $3$ datang daripada purata ke atas tiga asas Pauli, yang menghasilkan saluran penyahkutuban dengan parameter $\\frac{1}{3}$. Penganggar penuh kemudian difaktorkan sebagai hasil darab penganggar qubit tunggal. Seperti yang ditunjukkan dalam jadual, bagi $M$ observable, masing-masing dengan kelokalan $k$, bilangan bayangan Pauli yang diperlukan untuk menganggar semua observable kepada ralat aditif $\\varepsilon$ dengan kebarangkalian tinggi ialah $\\mathcal{O}(\\frac{3^k\\text{log}(M)}{\\varepsilon^2})$. Saiz sistem tidak menjejaskan kos pengukuran selagi observable kekal tempatan, jadi observable yang banyak secara eksponen boleh dianggar serentak dengan kos logaritma sahaja.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Median of means {#median-of-means}"
msgstr "Median bagi min {#median-of-means}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A plain mean over $T$ snapshots reduces the variance of a single-shot estimate of an observable as $\\frac{1}{T}$, but is sensitive to outliers. Median of means can be used to remedy this. The process involves the following:\n"
"- Splitting the $T$ snapshots into $K$ equally-sized groups\n"
"- Computing the mean within each group\n"
"- Returning the median across group means\n"
msgstr ""
"Min biasa ke atas $T$ snapshot mengurangkan varians anggaran satu-shot bagi sesuatu observable sebagai $\\frac{1}{T}$, tetapi sensitif terhadap outlier. Median bagi min boleh digunakan untuk mengatasi perkara ini. Prosesnya melibatkan perkara berikut:\n"
"- Memisahkan $T$ snapshot kepada $K$ kumpulan yang sama saiz\n"
"- Mengira min dalam setiap kumpulan\n"
"- Mengembalikan median merentasi min kumpulan\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial performs local Pauli shadow tomography to estimate properties of the GHZ state, first using a 10-qubit simulated example and then demonstrating a 100-qubit hardware experiment.\n"
msgstr "Tutorial ini melaksanakan tomografi bayangan Pauli tempatan untuk menganggar sifat keadaan GHZ, mula-mula menggunakan contoh simulasi 10-qubit dan kemudian menunjukkan eksperimen perkakasan 100-qubit.\n"

