# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Setup {#setup}"
msgstr "Persediaan {#setup}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following helper functions are used by the large-scale hardware example later in the tutorial:\n"
msgstr "Fungsi pembantu berikut digunakan oleh contoh perkakasan berskala besar kemudian dalam tutorial:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`bad_cz`, `bad_readout`, `bad_coherence` — Query the backend calibration data to identify gates, qubits, and edges that exceed error or coherence thresholds, so they can be excluded from the circuit layout.\n"
msgstr "`bad_cz`, `bad_readout`, `bad_coherence` — Menanya data penentukuran backend untuk mengenal pasti gate, qubit, dan tepi yang melebihi ambang ralat atau koheren, supaya ia boleh dikecualikan daripada susun atur litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`parallel_ghz` — Builds a GHZ circuit of a given size using a breadth-first search over the coupling map, spreading CNOT layers in parallel to minimize circuit depth.\n"
msgstr "`parallel_ghz` — Membina litar GHZ bagi saiz tertentu menggunakan carian pertama-lebar ke atas peta gandingan, menyebarkan lapisan CNOT secara selari untuk meminimumkan kedalaman litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`weighted_coverage`, `active_wires`, `z_trace_backward` — Compute how much of the GHZ circuit's error surface is protected by a given set of spacetime parity checks, using the backward-propagation technique from [[6]](#references).\n"
msgstr "`weighted_coverage`, `active_wires`, `z_trace_backward` — Mengira sejauh mana permukaan ralat litar GHZ dilindungi oleh set semakan pariti ruang-masa tertentu, menggunakan teknik perambatan ke belakang daripada [[6]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`add_measurements` — Appends GHZ-qubit and check-qubit measurements into separate classical registers so they can be postselected independently.\n"
msgstr "`add_measurements` — Menambah pengukuran qubit GHZ dan qubit semakan ke dalam daftar klasik yang berasingan supaya ia boleh dipilih pasca secara bebas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`build_shadow_circuits` — Produces one circuit per random Pauli basis by appending the appropriate single-qubit rotations before measurement.\n"
msgstr "`build_shadow_circuits` — Menghasilkan satu litar bagi setiap asas Pauli rawak dengan menambah putaran qubit tunggal yang sesuai sebelum pengukuran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`parse_hw_results_w_checks` — Unpacks the Sampler output into `(ghz_bits, check_bits, bases)` triples, one per shot.\n"
msgstr "`parse_hw_results_w_checks` — Menyahpek output Sampler kepada tiga serangkai `(ghz_bits, check_bits, bases)`, satu bagi setiap shot.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`adapt_to_flat_bits`, `estimate_zz_nn_hw` — Map the GHZ-register bits back into the full-device index space and compute the median-of-means $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$ estimate.\n"
msgstr "`adapt_to_flat_bits`, `estimate_zz_nn_hw` — Memetakan bit daftar GHZ kembali ke dalam ruang indeks peranti penuh dan mengira anggaran median bagi min $\\langle Z_i Z_{i+1}\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small-scale simulator example {#small-scale-simulator-example}"
msgstr "Contoh simulator berskala kecil {#small-scale-simulator-example}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, prepare a 10-qubit GHZ state using statevector simulation and estimate its properties using local Pauli shadows. The GHZ state is a maximally entangled quantum state with three or more qubits serving as a benchmark for multipartite entanglement. It is a common building block for quantum communication and cryptography protocols. Additionally, the GHZ circuit has fully known analytical properties, making it ideal for verification in this tutorial.\n"
msgstr "Pertama, sediakan keadaan GHZ 10-qubit menggunakan simulasi statevector dan anggarkan sifatnya menggunakan bayangan Pauli tempatan. Keadaan GHZ ialah keadaan kuantum terkait secara maksimum dengan tiga atau lebih qubit yang berfungsi sebagai penanda aras untuk keterkaitan multipartit. Ia ialah blok binaan biasa untuk protokol komunikasi kuantum dan kriptografi. Selain itu, litar GHZ mempunyai sifat analisis yang diketahui sepenuhnya, menjadikannya ideal untuk pengesahan dalam tutorial ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 1: Map classical inputs to a quantum problem {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"
msgstr "Langkah 1: Petakan input klasik kepada masalah kuantum {#step-1-map-classical-inputs-to-a-quantum-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prepare an ideal 10-qubit GHZ state.\n"
msgstr "Sediakan keadaan GHZ 10-qubit yang ideal.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Langkah 2: Optimumkan untuk pelaksanaan pada perkakasan kuantum {#step-2-optimize-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, define a function that collects shadow snapshots by rotating the GHZ state into random Pauli bases. This mirrors what the Sampler primitive does on hardware in the large-scale example.\n"
msgstr "Seterusnya, takrifkan fungsi yang mengumpul snapshot bayangan dengan memutar keadaan GHZ ke dalam asas Pauli rawak. Ini mencerminkan apa yang dilakukan oleh primitif Sampler pada perkakasan dalam contoh berskala besar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using Qiskit primitives {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"
msgstr "Langkah 3: Laksanakan menggunakan primitif Qiskit {#step-3-execute-using-qiskit-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this simulation, use the statevector directly.\n"
msgstr "Untuk simulasi ini, gunakan statevector secara langsung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process and return result in desired classical format {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"
msgstr "Langkah 4: Pasca-proses dan kembalikan hasil dalam format klasik yang dikehendaki {#step-4-post-process-and-return-result-in-desired-classical-format}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the shadow estimator and the median-of-means (MOM) estimator for the random measurement bases used to collect the shadow snapshots. Use these functions to estimate properties of the GHZ state, including single-qubit magnetization, two-qubit correlators, and the two-qubit RDM, from the collected measurements. Then compare the estimates with the exact values.\n"
msgstr "Takrifkan penganggar bayangan dan penganggar median bagi min (MOM) untuk asas pengukuran rawak yang digunakan bagi mengumpul snapshot bayangan. Gunakan fungsi ini untuk menganggar sifat keadaan GHZ, termasuk magnetisasi qubit tunggal, korelator dua qubit, dan RDM dua qubit, daripada pengukuran yang dikumpul. Kemudian bandingkan anggaran tersebut dengan nilai tepat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the results {#visualize-the-results}"
msgstr "Visualkan keputusan {#visualize-the-results}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first plot shows the estimated single-qubit magnetization values for the different qubits. The second plot shows the distribution of estimated two-point correlator values for all qubit pairs. The final plot shows the magnitude of the two-qubit reduced density matrix entries. A fairly large collection of snapshots is used for the given system size, so the results are close to the exact ones.\n"
msgstr "Plot pertama menunjukkan nilai magnetisasi qubit tunggal yang dianggar bagi qubit yang berbeza. Plot kedua menunjukkan taburan nilai korelator dua titik yang dianggar bagi semua pasangan qubit. Plot terakhir menunjukkan magnitud entri matriks ketumpatan terturun dua qubit. Koleksi snapshot yang agak besar digunakan untuk saiz sistem yang diberikan, jadi keputusan hampir sama dengan nilai tepat.\n"

